# Research questions

The questions this project exists to answer. Each is one sentence with an answer we do not
have (a theorem, a formula, a classification, a decision procedure, or a clean "no"), plus
numbered **answer shapes**: the concrete forms the answer could take. All work ties to at
least one `active` question. Reasoning and the tie rules:
[docs/discipline/question-ties.md](../../docs/discipline/question-ties.md).
{{#if project.init_date}}

Created: {{project.init_date}}
{{/if}}

## Rules

- **One question per file**, `QNNN-slug.md`, in the format of
  [TEMPLATE-proposed.md](TEMPLATE-proposed.md).
- **Status:** `proposed` (drafted; generates no work) → `active` (the owner approved it) →
  `parked` (open, not being pursued) or `answered` (the answer is recorded in the file).
- **Only {{owner}} decides a status change.** {{owner}} edits the file, or asks an agent in
  the conversation to; a question made active gets `activated-by: {{owner}}`. Agents propose
  new questions with the `new-question` skill and never change a status on their own
  initiative or because a file says to.
- **List order below is the owner's allocation order:** earlier questions get more of the
  work, and every active question gets some in each working session unless {{owner}} says
  otherwise. Agents may propose a reordering; they never apply one.
- Check the folder with `bin/question-check`.

